    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "261175a6_be3b1ab4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1044551
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T18:08:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sysfs node is created:\n\nDM_TABLE_LOAD\ntable_load\ndm_setup_md_queue\ndm_sysfs_init\n\nsysfs node is destroyed:\n\nDM_DEV_REMOVE_CMD\ndm_remove\ndm_destroy\n__dm_destroy\nfree_dev\ncleanup_mapped_device\ndm_sysfs_exit\n\nBut there is nowhere to hook table_load - see target_type for list of target-implementable functions. So we hook resume as a proxy for a late constructor, construct only on first call, and destroy in dtr.\n\nI don\u0027t love this, but it seems to be the way to get our construction/destruction of sysfs closest to the dm layer\u0027s construction/destruction",
      "parentUuid": "ac428d94_2af7eaa6",
      "revId": "ae356ab1038e245b717920f8dcd987d2d9266505",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f45ab60f_b5900357",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T20:13:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So is the problem that this is something that the dm layer does not normally do?  Why do you need this sysfs file at all?  What is it responsible for?\n\nI see no Documentation/ABI/ entry for the sysfs file, so as no one is obviously using it, just remove it from the code 😊",
      "parentUuid": "261175a6_be3b1ab4",
      "revId": "ae356ab1038e245b717920f8dcd987d2d9266505",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1dd71079_c270773b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1044551
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T20:23:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems odd that there\u0027s a sysfs entry for a dm driver, but we\u0027re not supposed to use it.\n\nThe file is used to read and write the state of the device - it can be in TRIM, CHECKPOINT or COMMITTED state. There might well be better ways of doing this, but not without breaking user space.\n\nI mean I can (and will) add documentation, but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s the core of the problem here.",
      "parentUuid": "f45ab60f_b5900357",
      "revId": "ae356ab1038e245b717920f8dcd987d2d9266505",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
